Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 08:04:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: employees headcount rendering as a concatenated number

The Summary card stripped every non-digit from executiveSummary.employees
and reformatted, so any string holding two figures became one absurd
number: "330,000 342,423" rendered as 330,000,342,423.

- utils: formatHeadcount parses the FIRST numeric group only; used by the
  Summary card, the PPTX export and the HTML export.
- claude.ts: normalise executiveSummary.employees server-side, preferring
  the FMP figure verbatim when available. The old range-stripper targeted
  financials.employees, a field that does not exist in the Part A schema,
  so it never ran.
- claude.ts: stop sending both the FMP and Wikipedia headcount to the
  model, and require a single number in the prompt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013o6GmY5zEJ8H8TyuAuqJiT
